{"name":"Peanut Brittle","hex":"#a6893a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peanut brittle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of brittle (confection) containing peanuts in a hard toffee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peanut_brittle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brittle (food)","blocks":[{"text":"Brittle is a type of confection consisting of flat broken pieces of hard sugar candy embedded with nuts such as pecans, almonds, or peanuts, and which are usually less than 1 cm thick."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Golden_peanut_brittle_cracked_on_a_serving_dish.jpg/330px-Golden_peanut_brittle_cracked_on_a_serving_dish.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brittle_(food)"},{"title":"Peanut","blocks":[{"text":"The peanut, also known as the groundnut, goober, goober pea, pindar or monkey nut (UK), is a legume crop grown mainly for its edible seeds, contained in underground pods. It is widely grown in the tropics and subtropics by small and large commercial producers, both as a grain legume and as an oil crop. Underground fruiting (geocarpy) is atypical among legumes, which led botanist Carl Linnaeus to name the species hypogaea, from Greek 'under the earth'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Arachis_hypogaea_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-163.jpg/330px-Arachis_hypogaea_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-163.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peanut"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Golden_peanut_brittle_cracked_on_a_serving_dish.jpg/500px-Golden_peanut_brittle_cracked_on_a_serving_dish.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Golden_peanut_brittle_